  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b1f72c88019dcc3196d2280d39cfd257</srcmd5>
    <version>1.7.0</version>
    <time>1786304497</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 1.7.0

- Add ChatOpenAIMantle for the Bedrock Mantle OpenAI-compatible API
- Support the reasoning_effort parameter for ChatBedrockConverse
- Use Anthropic simplified prompt cache management in ChatBedrockConverse
- Include the model name in invocation_params for Bedrock chat models

1.7.0 adds tests/unit_tests/chat_models/test_openai.py, which drives the new
ChatOpenAIMantle model through the python-langchain-tests ChatModel unit-test
bridge. That bridge is not packaged in Factory, so the module is added to the
existing --ignore list rather than the whole %check being dropped. Note the
langchain-aws[openai] extra itself IS satisfiable (python-langchain-openai
1.4.1 + python-openai 2.45.0); langchain-tests is the only blocker. No runtime
dependency is needed either way -- upstream defers the langchain_openai import
via __getattr__, so ChatOpenAIMantle only pulls it in on attribute access.

Built and verified on aarch64: 545 tests pass on both python313 and python314,
rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1370149</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c395a24321e8bf1048f632506eff36ed</srcmd5>
    <version>1.7.1</version>
    <time>1787241167</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-langchain-aws from 1.7.0 to 1.7.1.

Upstream changes:
- Add DynamoDBVectorStore, a vector store backed by DynamoDB vector
  indexes.
- Support streaming for Kimi models (moonshot/moonshotai providers) in
  ChatBedrockConverse.
- Refresh the bundled model profile data (openai.gpt-5.6-* Bedrock
  models now advertise a 1050000-token input limit).
- Strip AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK from the unit-test environment.

DEPENDENCY FLOOR / COORDINATION: upstream raised its boto3 floor from
1.43.32 to 1.43.64 and this spec follows it in both BuildRequires and
Requires. The floor is load-bearing, not cosmetic: DynamoDBVectorStore
calls DynamoDB's SearchVectors operation, which first appears in the
botocore service model in 1.43.64. The floor was NOT lowered to make
the build pass.

openSUSE:Factory currently carries python-boto3/python-botocore
1.43.36, so this package is unresolvable until the boto3/botocore
bump lands. python-boto3 1.43.72 and python-botocore 1.43.72 have
been submitted to devel:languages:python:aws (sr#1371286 for boto3,
sr#1371299 for botocore) precisely to unblock this. Please stage this
request together with those, or after they have reached Factory.

Local verification: built for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64 against a
repo layering the prepared boto3/botocore 1.43.72 over Tumbleweed;
%check runs the offline unit tests. No patches are carried.</comment>
    <requestid>1371318</requestid>
  </revision>
